{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0001_split_metadata_and_analytics_backends_decision", "label": "ADR 0001: Split Metadata and Analytics Backends", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-split-metadata-and-analytics-backends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Metadata stays in sqlite queried from TS via plugin-sql + Drizzle; parsing, Parquet conversion and Polars analytics live in Rust behind tauri::commands. All-Rust and all-TS were rejected: no duckdb/Polars equivalent on the webview side, no Python runtime for pandas, and the developer is not yet fluent in Rust, so only the part that genuinely needs Rust is written in it."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0001_split_metadata_and_analytics_backends_ipc_boundary", "label": "Structured-Params IPC Boundary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-split-metadata-and-analytics-backends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Structured params in, computed results out; never a raw SQL/query string across IPC, because Polars calls are Rust method chains rather than a string query language."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0001_split_metadata_and_analytics_backends_decision", "target": "docs_adr_0001_split_metadata_and_analytics_backends_ipc_boundary", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-split-metadata-and-analytics-backends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_split_metadata_and_analytics_backends_ipc_boundary", "target": "claude_invoker_pattern", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/adr/0001-split-metadata-and-analytics-backends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0001_split_metadata_and_analytics_backends_ipc_boundary", "target